  "explanation": [
    "PostgreSQL treats the four filters as independent. A tenth of the orders are from Reykjavik, a tenth are in Iceland, a tenth in krónur and a tenth in Icelandic, so it expected 100,000 × 0.1 × 0.1 × 0.1 × 0.1 = 10 rows. They are the same 10,000 orders. Expecting 10, it looked up each order's customer through customers_pkey: 4 × (10,000 + 10,000) = 80,000, and 100,000 in all. A hash join reads the 10,000 customers once instead: 10,000 + 20,000 for the join, 50,000 in all.",
    "PostgreSQL keeps statistics for each column on its own. Extended statistics tell it that the columns depend on each other: CREATE STATISTICS orders_place (dependencies) ON city, country, currency, language FROM orders, then ANALYZE orders."
  ]
